            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain and electrocardiographic ST-segment elevation occurring in the recovery phase after exercise in a patient with normal coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>228-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exercise-induced ST-segment elevation usually occurs in patients with coronary artery disease. We report a case in which ST-segment elevation occurred during the recovery phase of exercise in a patient with normal coronary arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
